        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Both orders give an even function. If $g$ is even, $h(-x)=f(g(x))=h(x)$. If $g$ is odd and $f$ is even, $h(-x)=f(-g(x))=f(g(x))=h(x)$.",
          "worked": "If $f$ is even and $g$ is odd, $$\\begin{align*}h(-x)&=f(g(-x))\\\\h(-x)&=f(-g(x))\\\\h(-x)&=f(g(x))\\\\h(-x)&=h(x).\\end{align*}$$ If $f$ is odd and $g$ is even, $$\\begin{align*}h(-x)&=f(g(-x))\\\\h(-x)&=f(g(x))\\\\h(-x)&=h(x).\\end{align*}$$ In both cases, $h$ is even.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
